{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"can-filter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Can-Filter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ability for a column to be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"globally"}]},{"type":"text","value":" filtered is determined by the following:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The column was defined a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorKey"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getColumnCanGlobalFilter"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for the given column. If it is not provided, the column is assumed to be globally filterable if the value in the first row is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.enableColumnFilter"},{"type":"text","value":" is not set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.enableColumnFilters"},{"type":"text","value":" is not set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.enableFilters"},{"type":"text","value":" is not set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filter state is stored on the table using the following shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export interface GlobalFilterTableState {\n  globalFilter: any\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"filter-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filter Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can use the same filter functions that are available for column filtering for global filtering. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guide/column-filtering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Filtering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to learn more about filter functions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"using-filter-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Filter Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filter functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.globalFilterFn"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a built-in filter function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function directly provided to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.globalFilterFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final list of filter functions available for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.globalFilterFn"},{"type":"text","value":" options use the following type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type FilterFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | BuiltInFilterFn\n  | FilterFn<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"filter-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filter Meta"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filtering data can often expose additional information about the data that can be used to aid other future operations on the same data. A good example of this concept is a ranking-system like that of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/kentcdodds/match-sorter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"match-sorter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that simultaneously ranks, filters and sorts data. While utilities like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"match-sorter"},{"type":"text","value":" make a lot of sense for single-dimensional filter+sort tasks, the decoupled filtering/sorting architecture of building a table makes them very difficult and slow to use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To make a ranking/filtering/sorting system work with tables, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn"},{"type":"text","value":"s can optionally mark results with a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"filter meta"}]},{"type":"text","value":" value that can be used later to sort/group/etc the data to your liking. This is done by calling the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" function supplied to your custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Below is an example using our own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"match-sorter-utils"},{"type":"text","value":" package (a utility fork of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"match-sorter"},{"type":"text","value":") to rank, filter, and sort the data"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { sortingFns } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\nimport { rankItem, compareItems } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\nconst fuzzyFilter = (row, columnId, value, addMeta) => {\n  // Rank the item\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n\n  // Store the ranking info\n  addMeta(itemRank)\n\n  // Return if the item should be filtered in/out\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n\n  // Only sort by rank if the column has ranking information\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!\n    )\n  }\n\n  // Provide an alphanumeric fallback for when the item ranks are equal\n  return dir === 0 ? sortingFns.alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-def-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Def Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enableglobalfilter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableGlobalFilter?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"global"}]},{"type":"text","value":" filter for this column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcanglobalfilter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanGlobalFilter: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the column can be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"globally"}]},{"type":"text","value":" filtered.  Set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable a column from being scanned during global filtering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"row-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"columnfiltersmeta","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFiltersMeta"}]},{"type":"code","value":"columnFiltersMeta: Record<string, any>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The column filters meta map for the row. This object tracks any filter meta for a row as optionally provided during the filtering process."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"filterfns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"filterFns?: Record<string, FilterFn>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This option allows you to define custom filter functions that can be referenced in a column's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option by their key.\nExample:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"declare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    myCustomFilter: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  filterFn: 'myCustomFilter',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  filterFns: {\n    myCustomFilter: (rows, columnIds, filterValue) => {\n      // return the filtered rows\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"filterfromleafrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFromLeafRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"filterFromLeafRows?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, filtering is done from parent rows down (so if a parent row is filtered out, all of its children will be filtered out as well). Setting this option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" will cause filtering to be done from leaf rows up (which means parent rows will be included so long as one of their child or grand-child rows is also included)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"maxleafrowfilterdepth","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxLeafRowFilterDepth"}]},{"type":"code","value":"maxLeafRowFilterDepth?: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, filtering is done for all rows (max depth of 100), no matter if they are root level parent rows or the child leaf rows of a parent row. Setting this option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" will cause filtering to only be applied to the root level parent rows, with all sub-rows remaining unfiltered. Similarly, setting this option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" will cause filtering to only be applied to child leaf rows 1 level deep, and so on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful for situations where you want a row's entire child hierarchy to be visible regardless of the applied filter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablefilters","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableFilters"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableFilters?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables all filters for the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manualfiltering","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualFiltering"}]},{"type":"code","value":"manualFiltering?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disables the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFilteredRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" from being used to filter data. This may be useful if your table needs to dynamically support both client-side and server-side filtering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfilteredrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFilteredRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getFilteredRowModel?: (\n  table: Table<TData>\n) => () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, this function is called "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once"}]},{"type":"text","value":" per table and should return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"new function"}]},{"type":"text","value":" which will calculate and return the row model for the table when it's filtered."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For server-side filtering, this function is unnecessary and can be ignored since the server should already return the filtered row model."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For client-side filtering, this function is required. A default implementation is provided via any table adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ getFilteredRowModel }"},{"type":"text","value":" export."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getFilteredRowModel } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"globalfilterfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"globalFilterFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"globalFilterFn?: FilterFn | keyof FilterFns | keyof BuiltInFilterFns","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The filter function to use for global filtering."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" referencing a "},{"type":"link","href":"#filter-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in filter function"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a custom filter functions provided via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"#filter-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom filter function"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onglobalfilterchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onGlobalFilterChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onGlobalFilterChange?: OnChangeFn<GlobalFilterState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, this function will be called with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updaterFn"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.globalFilter"},{"type":"text","value":" changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enableglobalfilter-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableGlobalFilter?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables the global filter for the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcolumncanglobalfilter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getColumnCanGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getColumnCanGlobalFilter?: (column: Column<TData>) => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, this function will be called with the column and should return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to indicate whether this column should be used for global filtering.\nThis is useful if the column can contain data that is not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":" (i.e. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getprefilteredrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreFilteredRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPreFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table before any "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"column"}]},{"type":"text","value":" filtering has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfilteredrowmodel-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFilteredRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table after "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"column"}]},{"type":"text","value":" filtering has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setglobalfilter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setGlobalFilter: (updater: Updater<any>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets or updates the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.globalFilter"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetglobalfilter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetGlobalFilter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetGlobalFilter: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"globalFilter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" state to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState.globalFilter"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" can be passed to force a default blank state reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getglobalautofilterfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGlobalAutoFilterFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGlobalAutoFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Currently, this function returns the built-in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includesString"},{"type":"text","value":" filter function. In future releases, it may return more dynamic filter functions based on the nature of the data provided."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getglobalfilterfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGlobalFilterFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGlobalFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the global filter function (either user-defined or automatic, depending on configuration) for the table."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"can-filter","text":"Can-Filter","level":2},{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"filter-functions","text":"Filter Functions","level":2},{"id":"using-filter-functions","text":"Using Filter Functions","level":4},{"id":"filter-meta","text":"Filter Meta","level":4},{"id":"column-def-options","text":"Column Def Options","level":2},{"id":"enableglobalfilter","text":"enableGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"column-api","text":"Column API","level":2},{"id":"getcanglobalfilter","text":"getCanGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"row-api","text":"Row API","level":2},{"id":"columnfiltersmeta","text":"columnFiltersMeta","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"filterfns","text":"filterFns","level":3},{"id":"filterfromleafrows","text":"filterFromLeafRows","level":3},{"id":"maxleafrowfilterdepth","text":"maxLeafRowFilterDepth","level":3},{"id":"enablefilters","text":"enableFilters","level":3},{"id":"manualfiltering","text":"manualFiltering","level":3},{"id":"getfilteredrowmodel","text":"getFilteredRowModel","level":3},{"id":"globalfilterfn","text":"globalFilterFn","level":3},{"id":"onglobalfilterchange","text":"onGlobalFilterChange","level":3},{"id":"enableglobalfilter-2","text":"enableGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"getcolumncanglobalfilter","text":"getColumnCanGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"getprefilteredrowmodel","text":"getPreFilteredRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getfilteredrowmodel-2","text":"getFilteredRowModel","level":3},{"id":"setglobalfilter","text":"setGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"resetglobalfilter","text":"resetGlobalFilter","level":3},{"id":"getglobalautofilterfn","text":"getGlobalAutoFilterFn","level":3},{"id":"getglobalfilterfn","text":"getGlobalFilterFn","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Can-Filter\n\nThe ability for a column to be **globally** filtered is determined by the following:\n\n- The column was defined a valid `accessorKey`/`accessorFn`.\n- If provided, `options.getColumnCanGlobalFilter` returns `true` for the given column. If it is not provided, the column is assumed to be globally filterable if the value in the first row is a `string` or `number` type.\n- `column.enableColumnFilter` is not set to `false`\n- `options.enableColumnFilters` is not set to `false`\n- `options.enableFilters` is not set to `false`\n\n## State\n\nFilter state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport interface GlobalFilterTableState {\n  globalFilter: any\n}\n```\n\n## Filter Functions\n\nYou can use the same filter functions that are available for column filtering for global filtering. See the [Column Filtering](../../guide/column-filtering.md) to learn more about filter functions.\n\n#### Using Filter Functions\n\nFilter functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `options.globalFilterFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in filter function\n- A function directly provided to the `options.globalFilterFn` option\n\nThe final list of filter functions available for the `tableOptions.globalFilterFn` options use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type FilterFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | BuiltInFilterFn\n  | FilterFn<TData>\n```\n\n#### Filter Meta\n\nFiltering data can often expose additional information about the data that can be used to aid other future operations on the same data. A good example of this concept is a ranking-system like that of [`match-sorter`](https://github.com/kentcdodds/match-sorter) that simultaneously ranks, filters and sorts data. While utilities like `match-sorter` make a lot of sense for single-dimensional filter+sort tasks, the decoupled filtering/sorting architecture of building a table makes them very difficult and slow to use.\n\nTo make a ranking/filtering/sorting system work with tables, `filterFn`s can optionally mark results with a **filter meta** value that can be used later to sort/group/etc the data to your liking. This is done by calling the `addMeta` function supplied to your custom `filterFn`.\n\nBelow is an example using our own `match-sorter-utils` package (a utility fork of `match-sorter`) to rank, filter, and sort the data\n\n```tsx\nimport { sortingFns } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\nimport { rankItem, compareItems } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\nconst fuzzyFilter = (row, columnId, value, addMeta) => {\n  // Rank the item\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n\n  // Store the ranking info\n  addMeta(itemRank)\n\n  // Return if the item should be filtered in/out\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n\n  // Only sort by rank if the column has ranking information\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!\n    )\n  }\n\n  // Provide an alphanumeric fallback for when the item ranks are equal\n  return dir === 0 ? sortingFns.alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `enableGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nenableGlobalFilter?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the **global** filter for this column.\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getCanGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanGlobalFilter: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column can be **globally** filtered.  Set to `false` to disable a column from being scanned during global filtering.\n\n## Row API\n\n### `columnFiltersMeta`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnFiltersMeta: Record<string, any>\n```\n\nThe column filters meta map for the row. This object tracks any filter meta for a row as optionally provided during the filtering process.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `filterFns`\n\n```tsx\nfilterFns?: Record<string, FilterFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom filter functions that can be referenced in a column's `filterFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    myCustomFilter: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  filterFn: 'myCustomFilter',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  filterFns: {\n    myCustomFilter: (rows, columnIds, filterValue) => {\n      // return the filtered rows\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `filterFromLeafRows`\n\n```tsx\nfilterFromLeafRows?: boolean\n```\n\nBy default, filtering is done from parent rows down (so if a parent row is filtered out, all of its children will be filtered out as well). Setting this option to `true` will cause filtering to be done from leaf rows up (which means parent rows will be included so long as one of their child or grand-child rows is also included).\n\n### `maxLeafRowFilterDepth`\n\n```tsx\nmaxLeafRowFilterDepth?: number\n```\n\nBy default, filtering is done for all rows (max depth of 100), no matter if they are root level parent rows or the child leaf rows of a parent row. Setting this option to `0` will cause filtering to only be applied to the root level parent rows, with all sub-rows remaining unfiltered. Similarly, setting this option to `1` will cause filtering to only be applied to child leaf rows 1 level deep, and so on.\n\nThis is useful for situations where you want a row's entire child hierarchy to be visible regardless of the applied filter.\n\n### `enableFilters`\n\n```tsx\nenableFilters?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables all filters for the table.\n\n### `manualFiltering`\n\n```tsx\nmanualFiltering?: boolean\n```\n\nDisables the `getFilteredRowModel` from being used to filter data. This may be useful if your table needs to dynamically support both client-side and server-side filtering.\n\n### `getFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetFilteredRowModel?: (\n  table: Table<TData>\n) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function is called **once** per table and should return a **new function** which will calculate and return the row model for the table when it's filtered.\n\n- For server-side filtering, this function is unnecessary and can be ignored since the server should already return the filtered row model.\n- For client-side filtering, this function is required. A default implementation is provided via any table adapter's `{ getFilteredRowModel }` export.\n\nExample:\n\n```tsx\nimport { getFilteredRowModel } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n})\n```\n\n### `globalFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\nglobalFilterFn?: FilterFn | keyof FilterFns | keyof BuiltInFilterFns\n```\n\nThe filter function to use for global filtering.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in filter function](#filter-functions))\n- A `string` that references a custom filter functions provided via the `tableOptions.filterFns` option\n- A [custom filter function](#filter-functions)\n\n### `onGlobalFilterChange`\n\n```tsx\nonGlobalFilterChange?: OnChangeFn<GlobalFilterState>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with an `updaterFn` when `state.globalFilter` changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table.\n\n### `enableGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nenableGlobalFilter?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the global filter for the table.\n\n### `getColumnCanGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\ngetColumnCanGlobalFilter?: (column: Column<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with the column and should return `true` or `false` to indicate whether this column should be used for global filtering.\nThis is useful if the column can contain data that is not `string` or `number` (i.e. `undefined`).\n\n## Table API\n\n### `getPreFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any **column** filtering has been applied.\n\n### `getFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after **column** filtering has been applied.\n\n### `setGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nsetGlobalFilter: (updater: Updater<any>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.globalFilter` state.\n\n### `resetGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nresetGlobalFilter: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **globalFilter** state to `initialState.globalFilter`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `undefined`.\n\n### `getGlobalAutoFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetGlobalAutoFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nCurrently, this function returns the built-in `includesString` filter function. In future releases, it may return more dynamic filter functions based on the nature of the data provided.\n\n### `getGlobalFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetGlobalFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the global filter function (either user-defined or automatic, depending on configuration) for the table.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Global Filtering APIs\nid: global-filtering\n---\n\n## Can-Filter\n\nThe ability for a column to be **globally** filtered is determined by the following:\n\n- The column was defined a valid `accessorKey`/`accessorFn`.\n- If provided, `options.getColumnCanGlobalFilter` returns `true` for the given column. If it is not provided, the column is assumed to be globally filterable if the value in the first row is a `string` or `number` type.\n- `column.enableColumnFilter` is not set to `false`\n- `options.enableColumnFilters` is not set to `false`\n- `options.enableFilters` is not set to `false`\n\n## State\n\nFilter state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport interface GlobalFilterTableState {\n  globalFilter: any\n}\n```\n\n## Filter Functions\n\nYou can use the same filter functions that are available for column filtering for global filtering. See the [Column Filtering](../../guide/column-filtering.md) to learn more about filter functions.\n\n#### Using Filter Functions\n\nFilter functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `options.globalFilterFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in filter function\n- A function directly provided to the `options.globalFilterFn` option\n\nThe final list of filter functions available for the `tableOptions.globalFilterFn` options use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type FilterFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | BuiltInFilterFn\n  | FilterFn<TData>\n```\n\n#### Filter Meta\n\nFiltering data can often expose additional information about the data that can be used to aid other future operations on the same data. A good example of this concept is a ranking-system like that of [`match-sorter`](https://github.com/kentcdodds/match-sorter) that simultaneously ranks, filters and sorts data. While utilities like `match-sorter` make a lot of sense for single-dimensional filter+sort tasks, the decoupled filtering/sorting architecture of building a table makes them very difficult and slow to use.\n\nTo make a ranking/filtering/sorting system work with tables, `filterFn`s can optionally mark results with a **filter meta** value that can be used later to sort/group/etc the data to your liking. This is done by calling the `addMeta` function supplied to your custom `filterFn`.\n\nBelow is an example using our own `match-sorter-utils` package (a utility fork of `match-sorter`) to rank, filter, and sort the data\n\n```tsx\nimport { sortingFns } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\nimport { rankItem, compareItems } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\nconst fuzzyFilter = (row, columnId, value, addMeta) => {\n  // Rank the item\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n\n  // Store the ranking info\n  addMeta(itemRank)\n\n  // Return if the item should be filtered in/out\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n\n  // Only sort by rank if the column has ranking information\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]!\n    )\n  }\n\n  // Provide an alphanumeric fallback for when the item ranks are equal\n  return dir === 0 ? sortingFns.alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `enableGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nenableGlobalFilter?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the **global** filter for this column.\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getCanGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanGlobalFilter: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column can be **globally** filtered.  Set to `false` to disable a column from being scanned during global filtering.\n\n## Row API\n\n### `columnFiltersMeta`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnFiltersMeta: Record<string, any>\n```\n\nThe column filters meta map for the row. This object tracks any filter meta for a row as optionally provided during the filtering process.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `filterFns`\n\n```tsx\nfilterFns?: Record<string, FilterFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom filter functions that can be referenced in a column's `filterFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    myCustomFilter: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  filterFn: 'myCustomFilter',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  filterFns: {\n    myCustomFilter: (rows, columnIds, filterValue) => {\n      // return the filtered rows\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `filterFromLeafRows`\n\n```tsx\nfilterFromLeafRows?: boolean\n```\n\nBy default, filtering is done from parent rows down (so if a parent row is filtered out, all of its children will be filtered out as well). Setting this option to `true` will cause filtering to be done from leaf rows up (which means parent rows will be included so long as one of their child or grand-child rows is also included).\n\n### `maxLeafRowFilterDepth`\n\n```tsx\nmaxLeafRowFilterDepth?: number\n```\n\nBy default, filtering is done for all rows (max depth of 100), no matter if they are root level parent rows or the child leaf rows of a parent row. Setting this option to `0` will cause filtering to only be applied to the root level parent rows, with all sub-rows remaining unfiltered. Similarly, setting this option to `1` will cause filtering to only be applied to child leaf rows 1 level deep, and so on.\n\nThis is useful for situations where you want a row's entire child hierarchy to be visible regardless of the applied filter.\n\n### `enableFilters`\n\n```tsx\nenableFilters?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables all filters for the table.\n\n### `manualFiltering`\n\n```tsx\nmanualFiltering?: boolean\n```\n\nDisables the `getFilteredRowModel` from being used to filter data. This may be useful if your table needs to dynamically support both client-side and server-side filtering.\n\n### `getFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetFilteredRowModel?: (\n  table: Table<TData>\n) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function is called **once** per table and should return a **new function** which will calculate and return the row model for the table when it's filtered.\n\n- For server-side filtering, this function is unnecessary and can be ignored since the server should already return the filtered row model.\n- For client-side filtering, this function is required. A default implementation is provided via any table adapter's `{ getFilteredRowModel }` export.\n\nExample:\n\n```tsx\nimport { getFilteredRowModel } from '@tanstack/[adapter]-table'\n\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n})\n```\n\n### `globalFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\nglobalFilterFn?: FilterFn | keyof FilterFns | keyof BuiltInFilterFns\n```\n\nThe filter function to use for global filtering.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in filter function](#filter-functions))\n- A `string` that references a custom filter functions provided via the `tableOptions.filterFns` option\n- A [custom filter function](#filter-functions)\n\n### `onGlobalFilterChange`\n\n```tsx\nonGlobalFilterChange?: OnChangeFn<GlobalFilterState>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with an `updaterFn` when `state.globalFilter` changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table.\n\n### `enableGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nenableGlobalFilter?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the global filter for the table.\n\n### `getColumnCanGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\ngetColumnCanGlobalFilter?: (column: Column<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with the column and should return `true` or `false` to indicate whether this column should be used for global filtering.\nThis is useful if the column can contain data that is not `string` or `number` (i.e. `undefined`).\n\n## Table API\n\n### `getPreFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any **column** filtering has been applied.\n\n### `getFilteredRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetFilteredRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after **column** filtering has been applied.\n\n### `setGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nsetGlobalFilter: (updater: Updater<any>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.globalFilter` state.\n\n### `resetGlobalFilter`\n\n```tsx\nresetGlobalFilter: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **globalFilter** state to `initialState.globalFilter`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `undefined`.\n\n### `getGlobalAutoFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetGlobalAutoFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nCurrently, this function returns the built-in `includesString` filter function. In future releases, it may return more dynamic filter functions based on the nature of the data provided.\n\n### `getGlobalFilterFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetGlobalFilterFn: (columnId: string) => FilterFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the global filter function (either user-defined or automatic, depending on configuration) for the table.\n"}
